HST Office: "Tìm tính năng…" (Search Commands, Shift+Esc) finds features typed without diacritics, including the HST add-on commands, and has a button on the Home tab of the ribbon.

- sfx2/source/commandpopup/CommandPopup.cxx, sfx2/inc/commandpopup/CommandPopup.hxx:
  - Matching is case-, diacritic- and NFC/NFD-insensitive: labels, menu paths, tooltips and the
    typed text are compared as search keys (ICU NFD, combining marks removed, case-folded, "đ"
    as "d", white space collapsed), so "chu ky" finds "Chữ ký số…" and "dinh dang" finds
    "Định dạng…".
  - Ranking: label starts with the text, then a word of the label starts with it, then the menu
    path ("Menu ▸ Submenu ▸ Item") contains it, then every typed word occurs in the menu path or
    the tooltip. (The upstream "starts with" pass looked for " / " in a path joined with " ▸ "
    and never matched.)
  - The add-on menus (Addons.xcu OfficeMenuBar, e.g. the HST menu of the bundled extension) are
    merged into the menu bar at runtime and are not part of the module menu bar settings, so the
    popup never listed them. They are now read from the configuration (localized titles, order
    as in the menu, Context filtered by the current module) and listed as "HST ▸ Văn bản hành
    chính…". Add-on commands have no SFX slot: they are offered when the frame has a dispatcher
    for them (queryDispatch), and run through the same dispatch as before.
- sw/sc/sd notebookbar.ui (Tabbed UI, the HST default): a "Search Commands" button
  (.uno:CommandPopup, magnifier icon, label of the command, "Tìm tính năng…" in the vi UI) in the
  right-hand block of the Home tab, which never collapses into the overflow menu: in HST Writer
  next to "Văn bản hành chính", in HST Sheets and HST Slides as a third row under the search
  icons. The .ui label is only a fallback required by the accessibility check.
- Shift+Esc stays the shortcut on every platform (also macOS: ⇧⎋, no system conflict).

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/runtime/check-feature-search.py (ribbon buttons, Shift+Esc, searches "chu ky",
"dinh dang", "van ban hanh chinh", "chuyen ma", "usb", Enter opens the ND 30 wizard, HST menu).
